{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr={'sourceInformation':{'date':'2026-11-06 04:43:53','source':'Bomb Squad (1982, Intellivision)','plan':'PLAN.md','genre':'Real-time puzzle / light simulation','perspective':'Fixed 2.5D city dioramas and near-overhead orthographic circuit workbench','tech':'my-3D2dge 0.89.1 full handoff; AI Hub protocol 1 / client 1.4.0; PeerJS 1.5.5; vanilla JavaScript, HTML, CSS, Web Audio','artDirection':'Original native pixel-rendered green PCBs, cyan traces, patterned components, municipal response crew and warm/cool city lighting','animation':'Native Humanoid rigs, tweens, particles and state-driven tools','audio':'Original code-synthesized electronic score, effects and two filtered gibberish radio voices; music default 10%; no audio files','online':'One to four cooperative technicians; Hub shared-world authority or standalone PeerJS WebRTC rooms; claims, shared evidence, code voting and snapshot synchronization','testing':'Headless deterministic checks; actual browser input; emulated gamepad and touch; offline audio synthesis; two-page WebRTC; official Hub harness; screenshots for visual review. Physical devices and listening unknown.','research':'Read original Blue Sky Rangers manual and creator-maintained history; inspected original circuit screenshot; inspected engine, Hub and PeerJS primary documentation.','environment':'Codex CLI (headless); Linux','model':'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort max','usage':'added on import'},'testingFeedback':['Six unique defects discovered and fixed so far in the build ledger. Current acceptance evidence is under evidence/.','Two critical defects so far: native scene occlusion and the Hub ended-state initialization.','The ordinary-action case solver and 1920×1080 workbench review caught rule and presentation defects.','The initial syntax-only check established parsing but could not reveal scene occlusion.'],'engineFeedback':['The full engine provides native materials, shaped assets, rigs, fixed-step headless advance, and a controller-readable settings shell.','Yes. A large depth-sorted work table and a background overlay covered the interactive board; native decals and explicit sorting fixed them.','The authoritative repair, evidence, recovery and cooperative command model.','Keeping native world projection, target selection and shell overlays consistent.','None. Original registries, decals, tweens and shell extension points were sufficient.','A documented interaction-surface helper for projected large boards and their target anchors would simplify this genre.'],'promptFeedback':['The source loop, exact output contract and real-input verification requirements made the target concrete.','The plan names a different model effort/context than the filled task; TASK.md supplied the run metadata.','Integrating recoverable repairs, deduction, native presentation and both network lifecycles into one artifact.','Keep the completion gates and allow verification evidence to be summarized in one generated report.'],'aiHub':{'name':'Bomb Squad All Wired Up','tagline':'Keep your nerve. Save the city.','description':'Repair hazardous circuits, read the hidden digit stencils and make the final disarm call. Three original city cases and a guided workbench support solo play or a cooperative response crew.','type':'Game','genre':'Puzzle','source':'Bomb Squad (1982)','series':'','players':'1–4','controls':'D-pad/WASD focus; Cross/Space or mouse apply/hold; L1/R1 or 1–4 tools; Square/E test; Triangle/R repeat; R2/Tab evidence; Options/Escape menu; assisted touch.','tags':['puzzle','co-op','pixel art','retro','comedy','top-down']}}\nopen('../exit-interview.json','w').write(json.dumps(r,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\nnode tools/verify.mjs browser controller touch audio\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
