{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_144","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,re\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('../exit-interview.json');r=json.loads(p.read_text());ledger=Path('docs/testing.md').read_text();issues=len(re.findall(r'\"'^'\"\\\\| D\\\\d+',ledger,re.M));critical=len(re.findall(r'\"'^'\"\\\\| D\\\\d+ \\\\| critical',ledger,re.M))\nr['sourceInformation']['tech']='Full my-3D2dge 0.89.1 (local native Shell focus fix); AI Hub protocol 1 / client 1.4.0; PeerJS 1.5.5; JavaScript, HTML/CSS, Canvas 2D and Web Audio.'\nr['sourceInformation']['animation']='Native Humanoid rigs, tweens, particles, animated cutter jaws, joint flow and state-driven tool motion.'\nr['sourceInformation']['online']='1–4 cooperative technicians: authoritative Hub shared-world dispatch or standalone secure PeerJS Cloud / WebRTC rooms, board claims, shared evidence, crew votes, crew replay and snapshot rejoin. Arbitrary NAT/TURN connectivity is unknown.'\nr['sourceInformation']['testing']='Unlimited headless tests and visual screenshots allowed. Used native deterministic advance, ordinary-input campaign, emulated standard pad, phone/tablet profiles, offline audio, real two-page WebRTC, official Hub harness, and Chromium/Firefox/WebKit. Physical devices, listening and first-time human pacing are unknown.'\nr['testingFeedback']=[f'{issues} unique game defects were discovered and fixed; the issue ledger records each check and repair.',f'{critical} were critical: board occlusion, Hub ended-state initialization, and a retained code-dial index that could break shorter replays.','Most helpful: the fresh ordinary-input campaign, which exposed code-dial carryover and HUD interception; actual Hub rounds also exposed short-dispatch pacing.','Least helpful: syntax-only checks. They confirmed parsing but could not detect hidden boards, blocked clicks or stale network views.']\nr['engineFeedback']=['Most useful: native shapes/materials, Humanoid rigs, fixed-step headless advance and the shared controller-readable shell.','Yes. Large sorted planes and a background overlay covered the board. Native decals and explicit sorting fixed it.','Built separately: the authoritative repair, evidence, recovery, heat, command validation and cooperative voting model.','Hardest: keeping world projection, native menus, input focus and online fuse time consistent.','Changed one native Shell.show focus-retention path: refreshing a screen now preserves its focused widget. The full gamepad practice disposal verifies it.','Add a documented interactive-board surface with projected, selectable terminal anchors.']\nr['promptFeedback']=['Most useful: the source-specific repair loop, exact artifact contract and requirement for real-input acceptance.','Confusing: PLAN.md names a different model effort/context; the filled TASK.md supplies the actual run metadata.','Hardest: integrating repair recovery, deduction, native presentation and two complete networking lifecycles.','Suggested change: include a machine validator for the filename and exit-report schema in the starting folder.']\np.write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2)+'\\\\n');print(json.dumps({'issues':issues,'critical':critical,'reportParsed':True}))\nPY\nbiome check --write src tools tests/model.mjs\nnode tools/verify.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"{\"issues\": 16, \"critical\": 3, \"reportParsed\": true}\nChecked 12 files in 17ms. Fixed 1 file.\nFAIL official Hub conformance: two, four impaired, host leave, authority-only server\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-044353__x07899e/work/Bomb-Squad-All-Wired-Up-Bomb-Squad-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-044353/tests/browser.py\", line 126, in hold_target\n    try:wait(page,'!!__wired.currentBoard()?.hold')\n        ~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-044353__x07899e/work/Bomb-Sq